module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.witness_outside_gate_closure_falsified_by_other_file

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data witness_outside_gate_closure_falsified_by_other_file: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "witness_outside_gate_closure_falsified_by_other_file" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a witness outside the gate closure is falsified by a change to a DIFFERENT file and never reds** (THE WITNESS IS DECLARED, COMPILES, AND WOULD DISCRIMINATE CORRECTLY — it is routed to `DeclinedOutsideGateClosure` because its module falls outside the import closure of the required gate prefixes, so the floor never prepares, offers or executes it. A later, unrelated change touches a file other than the witness's own file — a file the witness may even IMPORT — and that change FALSIFIES the property the witness was written to check. The witness never reds, because it never runs; the floor was green because it never looked. The harm is doubly silent: the witness was discovered and its existence is reported as a decline, so the census reads as coverage.)",

    "THE INVALID STATE is a claim that BINDS NO EXECUTION. Two distinct facts about the tree — a witness's authored assertion and a change's perturbation of that assertion's subject — are never joined, and no mechanism makes the join, because the first fact lives in a module the gate does not compile. The witness's file can be read, reviewed, and accepted while describing a property that the tree already does not satisfy the moment some OTHER file changes in a way that breaks it.",

    "WHY IT IS A CLASS AND NOT A SLIP: every ordinary signal is compatible with the dormant witness and none of them malfunctions. The witness compiles, its source looks correct, the floor is green, and the change that falsified it is a valid edit to a file the witness never mentions. A reviewer of EITHER change sees nothing to investigate — the witness's diff is empty, and the other change's diff does not name the witness. The only join is the one the reader makes across two edits, and nothing demands that join.",

    "SPECIMEN, ALREADY MEASURED AND REPAIRED, which is what makes this a class rather than a worry. `dag/test/claim/executor_privileged_operation_witness_test.dag` witness `witness_population_tracks_the_slot_roster` asserted a transcribed `+ 4` against the host-wide privileged-operation tail. The tail grew to five elements via an edit to `dag/gunbc/runner/runner_host_grants.dag` (d38d4aedcdd, #10525). The witness was `DeclinedOutsideGateClosure` — `executor_privileged_operation_witness_test` is not in `required_gate_prefixes` — so the ordinary floor never executed it. Changed-witness selection did not fire, because the witness's OWN FILE did not change; the file that BROKE IT did. The growth was invisible from the `+ 4` file alone, and the change to `runner_host_grants.dag` contained no reference to any witness. Repaired in gunbc#10895 by deriving the count through `let host_wide = runner_host_wide_privileged_operations(deploy: ...).length()` instead of transcribing it, and the repair only executed because that PR happened to also touch the witness's own file.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable, held by no mechanism — the specimen was caught only because the PR that happened to repair it (#10895) also happened to touch the witness's own file, which is an execution-path coincidence rather than a detector. The floor already computes the `declined_outside_gate_closure` census count, but aggregates it into `declined` without surfacing it as a distinguished signal, so the gap between witnesses discovered and witnesses executed is computed and discarded. Surfacing that count would be a cheap detector but is currently unbuilt, so no mechanism today fires on this class.",

    "HARM: a property asserted to hold of the tree is demonstrably false after a mechanically permitted change, and the first signal that it holds no longer is the next person who reads both files and notices the contradiction. That is not a gate on any cadence and not an instrument anyone scheduled. The harm is latent until the false property becomes load-bearing — relied on by a later change, cited as established in a review, encoded in policy that depends on its truth.",

    "DISTINCT FROM ITS NEIGHBOURS AND THE BOUNDARY IS LOAD-BEARING. `witness_module_absent_from_the_executed_set` describes a witness that IS correct and whose schedule membership was never decided — the defect is the roster failed to include it. Here the witness is CORRECTLY declined by the gate closure policy: its home module genuinely falls outside the required prefixes and there is no scheduling error. The defect is that the property it asserts is falsifiable BY a change the witness does not own, and the gate closure that correctly declines it also insulates it from ever discovering that falsification.",

    "`stale_claim_survives_its_own_correct_edit` describes a PROSE claim — an annotation, a rationale, a comment — that a correct edit elsewhere made false. The present class describes an EXECUTABLE WITNESS, which is a different harm model: the stale prose claim is silent until read, while the stale witness is silent because it was never given the chance to execute. A reader opening the stale witness file finds correct, discriminating source; nothing is wrong about the code. The defect is at the JOIN between the witness's gate membership and the falsifying change's scope, not in the witness's source.",

    "`witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red` describes a witness whose SOURCE cannot compile, so no run can evaluate it. Here the witness compiles and would execute its arms correctly if it ran — it simply never does, because its module is outside the gate's prepared subject. A compiler error on the witness would be a loud refusal; an unwitnessed falsification is silent.",

    "`check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim` describes a check whose OPERATIONAL SUBJECT is a strict subset of its DECLARED SUBJECT — the claim is about the whole tree but the check only examines part of it. The witness in this class is correct and operates on the right subject; it is the WITNESS ITSELF that is excluded from execution, not its subject narrowed.",

    "WHAT MAKES IT A CLASS AND NOT A ROSTERING-CODE DEFECT: the same shape recurs for every witness whose gate closure is tighter than the range of files whose changes could falsify its assertion. A witness about the compiler's treatment of patterns in the presence of import closures, filed in the module the closure resolves, is falsified when the interpreter changes its import-resolution behaviour in a file outside the gate closure. A witness about the floor's aggregate runtime, authored beside the floor, is falsified when a CI lane definition is shuffled into a file the floor witness never imports. The population is not one misconfigured prefix — it is the structural gap between a static closure and a dynamic perturbation surface.",

    "THE RECOGNITION RULE: ask what FILE CHANGES could make the witness's assertion false, and whether every such file is inside the gate closure that decides whether the witness runs. If the witness's own module is inside the closure but a change to a module it does not import could falsify it, the gate closure that correctly prepares the witness may still be too narrow to CATCH the falsifying change — and this row covers that case too, because the witness is discovered and may still not re-execute on a push that touches only the distant file. The trigger fires when the falsifying change's diff and the witness's execution set are disjoint.",

    "THE CHEAP DETECTOR NAMES A POPULATION THE FLOOR ALREADY COUNTS AND DOES NOT PRINT. Every `DeclinedOutsideGateClosure` identity is a witness the tree asserts and the floor never touches. Printing that count as a distinguished line in the floor verdict — `unexecuted_witnesses: N` — would give a reader a single number to ask about, and any non-zero number is a warning: N files claim something about the tree that the run's evidence does not speak to. That line already has a home: the floor's `declined_outside_gate_closure` census count, which today aggregates into `declined` and disappears. Surfacing it as its own signal is a rendering change, not a structural one.",

    "CEILING: 2, mechanically preventable — in this class the mechanism DETECTS rather than prevents: the false assertion stays writable and is exposed when a dependency changes. After transitive-dependency-based changed-witness selection lands, a witness outside the gate closure whose imported dependency changed WILL execute, and a false assertion WILL turn red. The invalid state (falsified assertion with no red) is therefore DETECTED every time its falsification source changes. But the state remains WRITABLE: an author can still commit a hardcoded literal against a dynamic count, and if the dependency happens not to change between commit and the author's review window, the witness stays green. And if the selection mechanism stops running or the witness drops out of the selected set, the class returns in full — §4b(2) defines rung 2 as exactly that condition. The ceiling is 2 rather than 3 (mechanically preventable in the ladder sense) because the defect is in the witness's source (a hardcoded literal), not in the dependency graph: transitive selection catches the symptom but does not prevent the root cause from being authored.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: transitive-dependency-based changed-witness selection — execute every witness whose TRANSITIVE DEPENDENCIES (the set of modules the witness's import tree reaches) overlap with the set of changed files in a push, regardless of whether the witness's OWN file changed. The dependency relation is decidable: it is the same Node-tree reachability the namespace authority already computes, so selection can be computed from the import graph rather than guessed. A witness outside `required_gate_prefixes` that would never run on an unchanged head runs when a dependency it imports (or a module that module imports) is touched. SUFFICIENT for every witness outside the gate closure. THE CAPABILITY is a changed-witness selector over the import graph, keyed to transitive rather than direct file change; the artifact is any witness whose dependencies changed appearing in the floor verdict.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
